Subject: [PATCH 6.6.y 0/2] can: isotp: backport of 2 patches that failed to
 apply to 6.6-stable

This resubmits "can: isotp: fix use-after-free race with concurrent
NETDEV_UNREGISTER" (commit 20bab8b88baac140ca3701116e1d486c7f51e311
upstream), which failed to apply to the 6.6-stable tree, together
with "can: isotp: serialize TX state transitions under so->rx_lock"
(commit cf070fe33bfbd1a4c21236078fadb35dd223a157 upstream) from the
same upstream series, which builds on it and would otherwise fail
for the same reason. This is the full set of 3 upstream isotp.c
patches from 7.2-rc3 minus the 1 already queued by the normal stable
process for 6.6 ("can: isotp: use unconditional synchronize_rcu()
in isotp_release()").

Unlike on 5.10.y/5.15.y/6.1.y, the dynamic max_pdu_size TX buffer
resize feature (commits 2f2dd39/973bb01) is already present here.
Patch 2/2 still needed one adaptation: the hrtimer_setup() API
consolidation is not yet present on 6.6-stable, so the new
so->echotimer is initialized with hrtimer_init()+.function= like the
other timers in isotp_init() on this branch. The actual race fixes
themselves are unaffected and fully applied. See each patch's
changelog for details.

Patch 1/2 ("fix use-after-free race with concurrent
NETDEV_UNREGISTER") is additionally adapted: upstream uses the
netdevice_tracker/netdev_hold()/netdev_put() debug-tracking infra,
which is not available on 6.6-stable. Replaced with the plain,
always-available dev_hold()/dev_put(), which is functionally
identical for the actual fix (holding a reference across a
concurrent NETDEV_UNREGISTER) - just without the extra leak-tracking
instrumentation. This mirrors the same adaptation made to the bcm.c
patch series and to isotp.c on 5.10.y/5.15.y/6.1.y, after an actual
build failure was reported there ("error: unknown type name
'netdevice_tracker'"); this revision has been verified with a clean
git am against a seeded net/can/isotp.c and no longer references
that type anywhere in the result.

This assumes the 1 already-queued isotp.c patch for 6.6-stable has
landed by the time this is applied. If not, please let me know and I
will rebase.

Oliver Hartkopp (2):
  can: isotp: fix use-after-free race with concurrent NETDEV_UNREGISTER
  can: isotp: serialize TX state transitions under so->rx_lock

